course: dictionary
lesson: 324
title: Anglican: a word for a church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anglican is a word for a type of church. Context helps you find its meaning. «The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA.» The sentence tells you that Anglican names a church, and that this church is in the USA.
explain: «Many Protestant and Anglican churches have women ministers and bishops.» Anglican is in the same list as Protestant, so it is another kind of church. An Anglican is a member of one of these churches. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Many Protestant and Church of England churches have women ministers" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: «In England, the local parish church is usually Anglican.» This means the parish church near you is usually part of the Church of England family. Anglican is an adjective (an Anglican church) and a noun (an Anglican, Anglicans). When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Anglican describes the Church of England and the churches around the world that grew from it.
fact: An Anglican is a member of one of these churches.
fact: Anglican churches have bishops and priests, and they use the Book of Common Prayer and hymns.
fact: The Anglican Communion is a worldwide family of churches, led spiritually by the Archbishop of Canterbury.
fact: «Episcopal» means led by bishops; «the Episcopal Church» is the Anglican church in the USA.
exercise: «The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA.» What does Anglican mean here? | A type of cake | *A church that grew from the Church of England, and is in the USA | A church led by the Pope in Rome | A church that grew from the Church of England
exercise: «The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA.» What does episcopal mean? | Very old | *Led by bishops | Led by children | Full of songs
exercise: Who leads the worldwide Anglican Communion spiritually? | *The Archbishop of Canterbury | The Pope | The head teacher of a school | The Prime Minister
test: What is an Anglican? | A person who sells bread | *A member of one of the churches that grew from the Church of England | A bird that lives on hills | A kind of old castle
test: «Catholic, Orthodox and some Anglican Christians pray for the dead.» What does pray for the dead mean here? | Sing loudly in the street | Cook dinner for the family | *Ask God to look after people who have died | Dig holes in the ground
exam: «Many Protestant and Anglican churches have women ministers and bishops; Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain only men.» Which churches ordain only men? | Many Anglican churches | Protestant churches | *Catholic and Orthodox churches | Episcopal churches
